# Composability

Frontend reviewers will look for composition, not copy-paste. One primitive, many call sites.

- Do not duplicate JSX, className stacks, or parse/fetch logic. Extract.
- Pages assemble. Shared look and behavior live in small components with typed props.
- Compose with `children` and slots. Do not grow a prop bag of booleans (`isLarge`, `showIcon`, `variant2`).
- A second copy is a bug. If you are about to paste, extract first.
- Clear UI atoms (hash, amount, narrative block, empty/error) are components from the first use — do not wait to see them twice.

```tsx
// ❌ same border + type soup in three files
<p className="border border-border text-secondary">{label}</p>

// ✅ compose
<Meta label={label} />
<Narrative>
  <Narrative.Lead>{lead}</Narrative.Lead>
  <Narrative.Meta>{meta}</Narrative.Meta>
</Narrative>
```

Keep each component one job. No kitchen-sink `FlexibleCard`.
